WEBVTT

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:24.420
Stop, please!
Don't go into <i>Nii-Nii</i>'s room!

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:28.970
I need cash, and I know
you hid my bank book in here!

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:30.680
Shut the hell up!

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:35.010
I didn't do anything to your bank book!
Don't mess up <i>Nii-Nii</i>'s room!

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:38.810
<i>Nii-Nii</i>'s gonna come back, and then--

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:38.810
I said, shut up!

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:52.770
<i>Nii-Nii! Nii-Nii!</i>

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:49.320
Ah, dammit!

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:52.780
If that leaves a mark,
they're gonna get all up in my shit!

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:02.920
Shut up! Stop shrieking
like a broken radio!

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:06.800
S-Stop it, you little shit!

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:09.420
You know, I've realized something.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:10.630
Oh?

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:14.050
This may have been
one of the worst fragments,

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:16.890
but looking back on it now,

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:22.480
it was quite the happy fragment,
as I was able to have Rika all to myself.

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:27.900
It's not uncommon for those who live in
loops to see a change in what they value.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:30.650
What was once tragedy is now joy.

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:33.860
I do quite like that.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.280
And? Do you like what you've become?

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:41.500
You may no longer be human--
nay, no longer Satoko Hojo.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:46.210
What a strange thing to proclaim, Eua-<i>san</i>.

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:50.380
I may be living in loops now,
but I am still myself.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:57.680
After all, I'm still chasing after that
happy world where I can live with Rika.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:01:59.600
Ah, yes.

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:31.980
HIGURASHI: WHEN THEY CRY SOTSU

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:35.610
No!

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:39.570
It's okay! I'm your friend, Satoko!

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:42.330
Save me! Save me!

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:47.750
I'm scared... I'm scared!

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:44.540
Satoko!

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:47.750
Sorry, Keiichi,
but you need to back off!

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:52.710
It's okay, Satoko-<i>chan</i>.
You don't have to be scared anymore.

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:57.420
<i>Nii-Nii</i>, please come save me!

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:54.750
You're okay.

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:02.470
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry...

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:06.350
We couldn't do anything to help you.

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:09.140
Please forgive us...

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:21.070
Wednesday, June 15th, 1983

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:38.380
Rika-<i>chan</i>!

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:39.590
Where's Satoko?

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:50.480
What the hell?! Why couldn't
Child Welfare Services help her?!

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:54.060
Satoko made a false report before...

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.900
So they won't do anything
without real proof.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:59.570
So what, just let her be abused
until she's bruised and scarred?!

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:02.570
Of course not! I'm just saying,
they need to be more careful--

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:04.660
Why the hell are you all
standing around doing nothing?!

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:08.870
Shion? Why are you here?!

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:11.670
Are you just going to wait
and let him kill Satoko?

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:13.830
We have to do something right now!

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:17.460
I agree with Shi-<i>chan </i>and Keiichi-<i>kun</i>.

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:20.050
We can't just wait and see what happens.

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:22.260
There must be something we can do!

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:26.180
What, though? Make another report
to Child Welfare Services?

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:29.020
Why do we have to go
through all that bullcrap?!

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:31.480
Let's just ambush the bastard
and beat him to a bloody, dead pulp!

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:42.200
I-Is this right?

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:47.330
What's next...? "Put the chopped
vegetables in the pan"?

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:42.360
{=0}Everyday Recipes

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:42.400
{=0}Everyday Recipes

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:42.530
{=0}Everyday Recipes

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:47.410
{=0}Everyday Recipes

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:51.200
"Add a teaspoon of oil"?

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:56.170
The hell is a "teaspoon"?

00:05:56.170 --> 00:06:00.300
Could ya make it any more
confusing, ya assholes?!

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:02.340
You just want me to add a "teaspoon"?!

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:09.220
How's this, then?!

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:12.390
Now <i>this </i>is cookin'!

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:15.600
What on Earth are you doing?!

00:06:16.940 --> 00:06:19.230
Satoko--

00:06:16.940 --> 00:06:19.230
Turn off the stove now!

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:23.400
S-Satoko?

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:28.370
My goodness, Uncle!
You very nearly burned the house down!

00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:32.660
Sorry... I just wanted
to surprise ya with somethin'.

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:35.960
Well, I'm certainly surprised!

00:06:35.960 --> 00:06:39.710
Still, whyever did you decide
to try to cook, Uncle?

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:44.930
I thought makin' something yummy
for ya might make ya feel better.

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:49.140
Thank you for the kind thought,

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:55.230
but what would happen if
the villagers reported this to CWS?

00:06:56.650 --> 00:07:02.150
We're the only people
we can trust in this whole village.

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:04.320
We can't show any weakness.

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:10.580
Hey, Satoko. You think I should
call CWS and try to explain things?

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:12.950
It's the two of us
versus the whole village.

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:16.460
Who do you think they'll listen to?

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:22.300
Besides, if the Sonozaki family gets
involved, CWS will do whatever they say.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:27.260
Ain't there anything we can do?

00:07:27.260 --> 00:07:30.220
I just wanna have a quiet,
happy life here with ya.

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:34.390
That's all I want.
Why won't they let us be?

00:07:37.230 --> 00:07:41.270
Come now, Uncle!
There's no use in fretting about it.

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:46.030
Let's get this kitchen
spic and span! I'll help.

00:07:46.030 --> 00:07:48.410
First, we'll need water and some rags!

00:07:48.410 --> 00:07:53.080
G-Good idea! Leave the liftin'
and scrubbin' to me!

00:07:59.710 --> 00:08:02.500
Here we are. We're doing this.

