00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:05.670
Yeah! We're gonna get Satoko-<i>chan </i>back!

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:07.010
Yeah.

00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:10.640
I know this goes without saying,
but be on your best behavior, yeah?

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:13.930
What they do next is up to us.

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:15.850
Let's head in already.

00:08:15.850 --> 00:08:18.770
If you're not going
to go with <i>my </i>idea,

00:08:18.770 --> 00:08:22.770
then you'd better
make this work, Kei-<i>chan</i>.

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:25.320
Got it. Let's do this!

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:30.450
Oh? Look at that...

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:32.030
See something, sir?

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:38.580
Oh, no, just wondering what
the Maebara boy's doing in there.

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:40.830
At Child Welfare Services?

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:46.800
He was also with the head of the Furude
family and the two Sonozaki sisters.

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:52.510
Would you look into that
for me later, Kuma-<i>chan</i>?

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:53.760
Of course, sir!

00:08:57.390 --> 00:09:00.100
Hey, Satoko, where do we put the...

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:33.300
Thursday, June 16th, 1983

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:37.010
Listen up, everyone!

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:40.350
I want to talk to
you guys about Satoko Hojo!

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:43.730
As you well know,
Satoko didn't come to school today.

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:01.000
What?

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:05.040
Uncle! Dinner's just about ready!

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:08.090
What's the matter?

00:10:08.090 --> 00:10:11.550
N-Nothing! Lemme go hang these up to dry!

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:21.390
Hey, you! What're you doing,
snoopin' about, huh?!

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:22.890
Bastards!

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:28.400
Can't let your guard down
around anyone here!

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:30.730
It's not just one person.

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:34.070
It's everyone in Hinamizawa.

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:37.160
Can I really not do anything to help?

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:41.080
Isn't there somethin' I can do?

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:45.120
Our club members already launched
a strike on the CWS center!

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:51.460
All they did was write down that
"five classmates asked us to protect her."

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:54.050
Do you know what that means?

00:10:54.050 --> 00:10:55.840
Five people isn't enough!

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:59.050
We need your help to save our friend!

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:03.100
Let's show 'em how strong
the Hinamizawa school spirit is!

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:07.020
What can I do?

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:10.400
How can I save Satoko from all this?

00:11:20.660 --> 00:11:23.250
Have a good one!

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:23.320
Sevens Mart

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:28.210
Is that right? Teppei Hojo's
back in Hinamizawa?

00:11:28.210 --> 00:11:30.630
Yes, and we're not sure why.

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:38.300
Knowing him, he probably got too drunk
and picked a fight with the wrong guy.

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:43.390
That, or he got greedy and went after
yakuza protection money.

00:11:44.390 --> 00:11:48.560
Either way, he's definitely not
hanging around Okinomiya anymore.

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:53.900
What do you think of the rumor that he's
keeping Satoko holed up in their house?

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:53.150
"Gifu Prefectural Police"

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:59.740
Maebara-<i>san </i>and his friends
could be blowing things out of proportion.

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:02.780
But seeing as I've arrested Teppei
more times than I can count,

00:12:02.780 --> 00:12:05.660
I wouldn't be surprised if he was.

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:08.750
I pity poor, little Satoko-<i>san</i>.

00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:11.590
Ooishi-<i>san</i>!

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:21.720
Well, well, fancy seeing you out here.

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:25.220
Wha--?!

00:12:27.770 --> 00:12:31.980
Hold on there, Hojo-<i>san</i>!
What are you trying to pull?

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:34.070
Hey! Cut that out!

00:12:34.070 --> 00:12:39.490
Hojo-<i>san</i>, do you need something from me?

00:12:39.490 --> 00:12:44.830
Please, Detective! I need your help
with somethin' real important!

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:49.040
It must be serious if you're going
to make this much of a fuss about it.

00:12:53.880 --> 00:12:55.170
Very well.

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:57.880
Could you stand up, please?

00:12:57.880 --> 00:13:01.300
You're not in any position
to be asking favors of me,

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:05.600
but who am I to deny a guy
down on his knees asking for help?

00:13:08.810 --> 00:13:11.560
I'm back, Satoko!

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:14.230
Welcome home, Uncl--

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:16.900
Hello there.

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:20.650
Well, well, you <i>did</i>
come back to this old place.

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:25.160
I can't say I've ever seen
the two of you together, Uncle.

00:13:25.160 --> 00:13:26.950
Whatever is going on?

00:13:26.950 --> 00:13:30.660
Just figured we needed
some allies to help keep you safe.

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:33.790
I wouldn't call me an ally just yet.

00:13:33.790 --> 00:13:39.210
All you've asked of me is to come by
your home. I haven't heard the story yet.

00:13:39.210 --> 00:13:41.380
I'll admit...

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:47.180
From the look of this place,
things aren't as bad as reported to CWS.

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:51.020
Let me explain everything to ya first.

00:13:53.900 --> 00:13:56.730
The village is bullying her?

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:00.360
Can't say I believe that...

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:03.660
I know, you can't believe a word I say!

00:14:03.660 --> 00:14:05.870
But you'll believe Satoko!

00:14:05.870 --> 00:14:11.660
Everything he said is true. My uncle is
the only person I have on my side.

00:14:13.710 --> 00:14:18.800
The villagers I pass by,
my classmates, everyone--

00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:21.840
they all say I'm an "enemy."

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:26.850
Mind if I take a look around the place?

00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:40.280
Don't see any clues of you
being locked up in here or abused.

00:14:51.080 --> 00:14:55.580
And it doesn't look like
you're not being treated well.

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:57.580
Of course it doesn't.

00:14:57.580 --> 00:15:01.960
My uncle isn't harming me
in any way, shape, or form.

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:03.550
My apologies.

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:14.100
I can't believe my uncle
asked Ooishi-<i>san </i>to help.

00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:19.940
He believed my lie, <i>and </i>went
that far to help me? I'm shocked.

00:15:59.770 --> 00:16:03.110
I'm so sorry, Ooishi-<i>san</i>.

00:16:03.110 --> 00:16:09.070
You've tried so hard to solve the
Hinamizawa murders, but never succeeded.

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:11.370
But not to worry.

00:16:11.370 --> 00:16:17.870
This medicine will open your eyes
to the truth you so desire.

00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:28.720
What tragedy will Ooishi
bring about when he reaches L5?

00:16:28.720 --> 00:16:31.260
I must say, I'm enthralled.

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:37.640
It will certainly be a sight
to stave off our boredom.

00:16:39.020 --> 00:16:41.190
Wouldn't you agree?

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:45.900
My apologies for staying so late.

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:48.110
So will you help Satoko?

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:54.490
From what I saw, there was nothing here
that would warrant a call to CWS.

00:16:54.490 --> 00:16:55.660
So you will!

00:16:55.660 --> 00:17:01.710
I can't say or do much out in the public
eye, what with my being a public servant,

00:17:01.710 --> 00:17:07.010
but if anything changes at all,
or you feel like you might be in danger,

00:17:07.010 --> 00:17:09.170
call me right away.

00:17:09.170 --> 00:17:13.640
I promise I'll do what I can to help.

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:15.930
I owe you my life!

00:17:16.810 --> 00:17:22.020
I couldn't ask for a better ally
to have on my side than you, Ooishi-<i>san</i>.

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:24.440
Oh, now you're just flattering me.

00:17:25.730 --> 00:17:28.240
Right then, call me.

00:17:47.960 --> 00:17:50.090
<i>Oyassan...</i>

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:53.840
Every year, I promise
I'll finally avenge you.

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:58.770
I promised at your grave
that I'd find your missing arm.

00:17:58.770 --> 00:18:01.480
This year, I'll do it.

00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:04.850
I might be able to get close
to the criminals behind the curse.

00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:08.780
Though i won't be doing it by the book!

00:18:17.160 --> 00:18:19.490
Ooishi-<i>san</i>!

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:23.830
Sorry for the long wait.
I hope you're not mad at me, Kuma-<i>chan</i>.

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:25.580
No, I'm used to it.

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:29.000
So what was it that Teppei Hojo
wanted from you?

00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:33.800
I'll have to tell you later, Kuma-<i>chan</i>.

00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:37.260
Speaking of which, has anything
happened at Child Welfare Services?

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:41.930
They went to petition for her again
today--a bigger crowd than last time.

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:45.310
Maebara-<i>san</i>'s only just
moved here, after all.

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:50.230
He might've been convinced to join in with
the bullying without knowing what it is.

00:18:50.230 --> 00:18:51.360
Bullying?

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:55.490
Kuma-<i>chan</i>, I hate to ask this of you,
but could you wait here a little bit?

00:18:55.490 --> 00:18:58.780
Again? Sure, but where are you going now?

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:03.000
I'd like to walk around the village
and go up to the Furude Shrine.

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:06.750
Oh, right, Watanagashi is coming up.
Scoping out security?

00:19:06.750 --> 00:19:08.710
Yes, just that.

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:15.130
I want to make sure the places that are
most likely associated with the curse

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:17.140
are kept well and secure.

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:23.180
I couldn't believe it. I never thought
I'd see him hangin' up laundry.

00:19:23.180 --> 00:19:28.650
He sure was scary yellin' at us, though.
Guess that'll never change about him.

00:19:28.650 --> 00:19:29.980
Hello there.

00:19:29.980 --> 00:19:32.780
Why, if it ain't Ooishi-<i>san</i>!
How can we help ya?

00:19:32.780 --> 00:19:40.160
I just went by the Hojo house
and heard Teppei screaming at someone.

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:43.290
I'm not surprised.

00:19:43.290 --> 00:19:48.250
Y'see, we've also heard
that rumor goin' around--

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:49.710
'bout what's happenin' to poor Satoko.

00:19:49.710 --> 00:19:51.170
Is he abusing her?!

00:19:51.170 --> 00:19:53.380
We think so, but there's no proof.

00:19:53.380 --> 00:19:56.880
Can't you do somethin' about it?

00:19:58.220 --> 00:20:01.970
Sadly, I'm not allowed
to interfere in civil matters.

00:20:01.970 --> 00:20:08.350
Though if you wouldn't mind,
would you keep an eye on them for me?

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:09.810
I suppose.

00:20:58.610 --> 00:21:00.360
Good evening to ya, Detective.

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:03.620
Hello there. Workin' up a sweat?

00:21:03.620 --> 00:21:06.540
Have you seen Teppei around?

00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:10.960
What? You mean the Hojo guy?
No, haven't seen 'im.

00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:14.960
Is that so? He was just here.

00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:20.050
I saw him running away
from the shrine just now.

00:21:20.050 --> 00:21:21.720
Teppei was up there?

00:21:21.720 --> 00:21:25.760
He certainly wasn't prayin' to
Oyashiro-<i>sama</i>, so what was he doing?

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:27.720
No idea.

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:31.270
Hope he's not stealing
from the offering box.

00:21:32.770 --> 00:21:39.360
There's no doubt about it now,
is there, my dear murderers?

00:21:40.700 --> 00:21:48.040
You have the perfect target for your
demoning away--for Oyashiro-<i>sama</i>'s curse.

00:21:48.700 --> 00:21:51.200
Friday, June 17th, 1983

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:53.630
Who would do something like this?

00:21:53.630 --> 00:21:57.170
From what I heard, Teppei kicked it over,

00:21:57.170 --> 00:21:59.710
then relieved himself
on the <i>torii </i>shrine gate...

00:21:59.710 --> 00:22:02.130
The gall of that man!

00:22:02.130 --> 00:22:06.430
You know what everyone's saying
about this year's curse, right...?

00:22:06.430 --> 00:22:07.680
Yeah.

00:22:07.680 --> 00:22:09.850
It'll hit the Hojos, no doubt about it.

00:23:41.980 --> 00:23:46.980
Tatariakashi-hen:
Curse-Revealing Chapter, Part 4

00:23:42.820 --> 00:23:46.860
Next time: "Tatariakashi-hen:
Curse-Revealing Chapter, Part 4."
